      "description": "Careers and Internships | William Jewell College facebook threads instagram youtube pinterest linkedin link tiktok radio radio-selected play pause send location Skip to Content Employees Students Parents Community Alumni Giving Admissions Find Your Purpose.  Find Your Place. Try Major Match Tool Admissions Admissions Explore admissions resources for every type of student, from first-year applicants and transfers to graduate, international, online and accelerated nursing students. Apply Visit Admission Guide First-Year Students Graduate Students Transfer Students Online Students International Students Nursing Accelerated Track Refer a Student Apply Now Aid & Scholarships Find Your Purpose.  Find Your Place. Try Major Match Tool Aid & Scholarships Aid & Scholarships Explore tuition, scholarships, cost estimates and financial aid resources to help you plan for college with confidence. Tuition & Fees Scholarships Talent Scholarships Loans Financial Aid Services Cost Calculator Student Employment Apply Now Academics Find Your Purpose.  Find Your Place. Try Major Match Tool Academics Academics Explore our majors, programs, study abroad opportunities and internships offered at William Jewell. Major Match Tool Majors & Programs Undergraduate Research Music Support and Accessibility Services Study Abroad 3-Year Degree Careers and Internships Honors Apply Now Life at Jewell Find Your Purpose.  Find Your Place. Try Major Match Tool Life at Jewell Life at Jewell Explore admissions resources for every student path, from applying and visiting to finding the right guide for your next step. Student Housing Clubs & Organizations Greek Life Music Cardinal Athletics Student Wellness Spiritual Life Liberty and Kansas City Apply Now About Find Your Purpose.  Find Your Place. Try Major Match Tool About About Explore our story, values, outcomes, accreditation, and support services to learn what shapes our campus community. Our Story Our Values Outcomes & Accolades Center for Faith and Culture Accreditation Leadership Reimagined Jewell Apply Now Get Started Get Started Contact Visit Apply Employees Students Parents Community Alumni Giving Apply Now Get Started Close Get Started Close Contact Visit Apply Search Search Menu Close What are you searching for? Search Close search area Career Development and Internships We’re here to help you with the lifelong process of career development and decision-making. We provide resources, opportunities and professional experiences to meet your career goals and encourage you to explore not only your interests, but also your values. Outcomes Resources Resources Contact Info Marissa Bland, Director 816-415-5938 blandm@william.jewell.edu Follow Us facebook twitter instagram linkedin youtube tiktok threads photos Beyond the Classroom Not all of life’s most important lessons are learned within the confines of a classroom, and we know that. We’re dedicated to developing true critical thinkers, and that includes the expansion of learning opportunities and meaningful life experiences. In addition to our academic Core Curriculum, we offer various programs to reflect that way of thinking. Pursue an internship with one of our many community partners. Collaborate with professors or your peers to complete original research and present on Colloquium Day. Use your classroom knowledge and passion to serve a local nonprofit. Whatever it may be, we’re here to help you accomplish it. Careers Career Preparation and Guidance From job fairs to mock interviews, resume writing and professional development, we will help with the transition from Jewell to your next chapter. We offer self-assessment tools that can direct your choice of majors or careers, and we help coordinate internship programs. Unsure of your career path? Join our career mentor program and get a firsthand look inside an industry from a seasoned professional. Career Development Opportunities Get a head start on your career and gain valuable experience by participating in a college internship in Kansas City. We offer self-assessment tools to help guide your choice of majors or careers, and we coordinate internship and mentoring programs. 2025 Grad Stories Career Mentor Program The Career Mentor Program , a cooperative with the Career Development Office and the Alumni Board of Governors, is offered for two months each semester (September-November and February-April). This program is a great way to gain valuable insight to business and industry. The Senior Experience An in-depth program for seniors, Life After Jewell , offers insights into personal, financial and professional success for life after graduation. Attend a workshop on using LinkedIn or session about preparing for graduate school. We even host a dining etiquette lunch and learn session. Service Learning Service learning is curriculum based, providing ways for you to be actively involved in service that is integral to your learning. The goal of service learning is to enhance knowledge gain, engage critical thinking and reflection and promote concern for the common good. The focus of the service component is individuals and communities that represent the diversity inherent in the world. Service learning is not only service to the community, but includes a learning component so that specific coursework is incorporated into the service and supplemented with ongoing reflection. The purpose of service learning is to give you the opportunity to apply your skills and coursework while providing a meaningful service to the local community and meeting course objectives. Service learning is different from… Volunteerism , where the primary emphasis is on the service being provided and the primary intended beneficiary is clearly the service recipient. Community Service , where the primary focus is on the service being provided as well as the benefits the service activities have on the recipients. The students receive some benefits by learning more about how their service makes a difference. Internships that engage students in service activities primarily for the purpose of providing students with hands-on experiences that enhance their learning or understanding of issues relevant to a particular area of study. Field Education , which provides students with co-curricular service opportunities that are related, but not fully integrated, with their formal academic studies. Students perform the service as a part of a program that is designed primarily to enhance students’ understanding of a field of study, while also providing substantial emphasis on the service being provided. Internships Just 15 miles from downtown Kansas City, Jewell has connections with successful alumni, entrepreneurs, business leaders and nonprofit organizations among the metro’s 82,000 employers. Get a head start on your career and gain valuable experience by participating in a college internship. HandShake Portal Advertising, Communication and Marketing Discover where creativity and strategy intersect and implement your classroom knowledge into real-world applications with marketing and publishing opportunities. Anthem Publishing Barkley Boston Magazine Image Impact MMGY Global RCA Group, Inc. Target Direct Marketing Arts Demonstrate how your artistic talent thrives in the professional sphere by working for arts and theatre organizations. Some recent student arts internships include: Arts Council of Metropolitan Kansas City Harriman-Jewell Series Lyric Theater – Kansas City Starlight Theater – Kansas City Sundance Institute Business and Consumer Products Finance Understand how your classroom studies transfer to the real world through internships with banks, consultants and other financial institutions. BankLiberty Carlyle and Associates Cochran Head & Co. Ernst & Young Hammond Financial KPMG Mariner Wealth Northwestern Mutual PriceWaterhouseCoopers LLP State Street Corporation UMB Waddell & Reed Government A valuable learning experience for almost any major at William Jewell College, government internships supply you with firsthand knowledge about the intricacies of government agencies and departments. Some recent government internships: Federal Bureau of Prisons Federal Reserve Bank of Kansas City State of Missouri U.S. Department of Agriculture U.S. Department of Commerce U.S. Department of Health and Human Services Health and Wellness Learn more about providing care in a variety of healthcare settings. Your major in health and wellness can take you to student internships within Kansas City or even around the world. Some recent health and wellness internships: Ayurveda Clinic – Pune, India Children’s Mercy Hospital Children’s Therapeutic Learning Center Crossroads Hospice Metropolitan Organization to Counter Sexual Assault (MOCSA) University of Kansas Medical Center Nonprofits, Charities and Organizations Whether you participate in nonprofit college internships in Kansas City or elsewhere, you’ll gain an understanding of how these organizations work and how they can yield a fulfilling career. Some recent nonprofit & charitable organization internships: Big Brothers/Big Sisters Boy Scouts of America Camp Quality – Greater Kansas City Chapter Cape Cod Foundation City Union Mission Conflict Resolution Center of Minnesota Ewing Marion Kauffman Foundation Greater Kansas City Community Foundation Harvesters Community Food Network International Visitors Council Israeli Institute for Democracy in Jerusalem National Archives – Kansas City People to People International Ronald McDonald House Charities Special Olympics Susan G. Komen Foundation Truman Heartland Community Foundation YMCA of Greater Kansas City Sports Many of our Jewell athletes translate their experience to summer internships for college students. Some recent sports internships: Charlotte Hornets Kansas City Chiefs Kansas City Monarchs (formerly T-Bones) National Football League Sporting Kansas City Technology and Consumer Services Complete an internship with some of the finest technology companies in Kansas City, in the country and around the world. Some recent technology and consumer service internships include: Burns and McDonnell Oracle Charles F. Curry Company Enterprise eShipping Evans Medical Distribution Garmin Global Gardens Hallmark Cards, Inc. Hertz Corporation Rolls-Royce Softwaregroup LLC TOMS Unilever Duke Colloquium The David Nelson Duke Colloquium is a long-time campus tradition, giving you the opportunity to present scholarly and creative works to faculty, staff and the community. Celebrating the Life of the Mind The Colloquium concept increases involvement of students in research, which William Jewell College believes to be a hallmark of an excellent liberal arts college. Colloquium Day is held each April on campus and is named for Dr. David Nelson Duke (1950-2000), who joined William Jewell’s religion faculty in 1980. During his 20-year career at Jewell, Dr. Duke proved himself as theologian, scholar, teacher and social advocate. His articles and books, community activism, collegiality and overall passion for life made naming the Colloquium in his memory a natural choice. We held our 2026 Colloquium in April. Students presented on a variety of topics: Presentation Abstracts Have More Questions? Get in contact with us! We’d be happy to provide more information about our career development opportunities in Missouri. Contact Us Major Match Tool Jump To: General Information 816.781.7700 Office of Admission 816.415.7511 Address 500 College Hill Liberty, MO 64068 About Virtual Tour & Map News & Media Event Calendar Athletics Music Find Office Directory Academic Calendar Employment Site Map Policies Policy Library Student Consumer Information Website Accessibility Policy Privacy Policy William Jewell College does not discriminate on the basis of age, disability, gender, genetic information, national origin, race/color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status or any other status protected by law (col